  "about": "MM3D (USA rev 1) draws its button prompts as 3DS art; each cell below, in the texture's own pixels [x0, y0, x1, y1], is drawn as port-assets' Xbox pad glyph for the pad button the app binds there (A/B/X/Y by name, L/R the triggers, ZL/ZR the bumpers, START the menu button, the circle pad the left stick). inlay: the prompt sits on a button face, which is filled in under the glyph. scale: no texture pack covers these, so the game's own art is enlarged this much. A texture in a GAR archive is <archive>.gar/<file>.",
